cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. Figures derived from
  ENTSO-E data must also name the ENTSO-E Transparency Platform as their
  source, under its terms of use.
type: software
title: "Grid Carbon Intensity: hourly carbon intensity of electricity in DE-LU and France, with its uncertainty"
abstract: >-
  Carbon intensity of electricity generation for the DE-LU and FR bidding
  zones, 2021-2025, at hourly and quarter-hourly resolution, derived from the
  ENTSO-E generation mix and published life-cycle emission factors (IPCC AR5,
  and Itten et al. 2023 for German lignite and hard coal), with a 90 % Monte
  Carlo interval on every step and year and the share of each fuel's factor
  in its variance. Ingestion with an append-only raw layer and SHA-256
  manifest, DuckDB and dbt from staging to marts, and checks against
  Fraunhofer ISE's Energy-Charts and SMARD. Work in progress: the
  load-shifting decision model is designed but not yet run.
authors:
  - family-names: Olagoke
    given-names: Adewole
repository-code: "https://github.com/aolagoke-dsae/grid-carbon-intensity"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - carbon intensity
  - electricity
  - ENTSO-E
  - life-cycle assessment
  - uncertainty quantification
  - Monte Carlo
  - dbt
  - DuckDB
